---
import Shell from '../../layouts/Shell.astro';
import Tiles from '../../components/Tiles.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<Shell title="Foundations" section="foundations" prose={false} description="The decisions everything else in ERA is built on.">
  <h1 class="display">Foundations</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    The decisions everything else rests on. Each page here is rendered from the live tokens, so none of it can quietly
    go out of date.
  </p>

  <Tiles />

  <hr class="rule" />

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>How they fit together</h2>
    <p>
      Colour, type, spacing and shape are not four separate systems. They share one structure: a raw scale that never
      changes, a brand layer that picks from it, and a semantic layer that says what each choice is for. The
      <a href={`${base}/tokens`}>token page</a> walks that chain end to end.
    </p>
    <p>
      Two of these change per brand and two do not. Typeface and corner treatment are brand decisions. The spacing grid
      and the type scale are the same everywhere, because a brand that needs its own spacing scale is really a second
      design system.
    </p>
  </div>
</Shell>
